        "original_id": "b342d871-e203-5202-a7ea-1e331d95326f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Scottish Maritime Museum\n- Places: Clydebuilt, Braehead, Renfrew, River Clyde, Renfrewshire\n- Events: museum opening, museum closure\n\nFacts:\n- Clydebuilt at Braehead originally opened in 1999 as a third museum of the Scottish Maritime Museum.\n- Clydebuilt at Braehead was closed indefinitely in October 2010 because of lack of funding.\n- Braehead is a commercial development on the former site of Braehead Power Station in Renfrew.\n- Braehead is on the south bank of the River Clyde in Renfrewshire.\n- Braehead is rendered as \"Braeheid\" in Scots and \"Ceann a' Bhruthaich\" in Gaelic.",
